From: Aurora Silicon <hey@djdev.me>
Subject: [PATCH] CPU/GPU: recognize the A18 Pro chip

Backport the T8140 name already present in fastfetch 2.69.0. The shared
lookup also supplies the Asahi DRM GPU name instead of inferring an M-series
name from GPU architecture generation.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/blob/2.69.0/src/detection/cpu/cpu.c]

diff --git i/src/detection/cpu/cpu.c w/src/detection/cpu/cpu.c
index a796175..24afa35 100644
--- i/src/detection/cpu/cpu.c
+++ w/src/detection/cpu/cpu.c
@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@ const char* ffCPUAppleCodeToName(uint32_t code) {
             return "Apple M4 Pro";
         case 6041:
             return "Apple M4 Max";
+        case 8140:
+            return "Apple A18 Pro";
         default:
             return nullptr;
     }
